{
  "name": "a1",
  "procedures": {
    "notes": [
      "HOW THIS FILE STAYS ROBOT-INDEPENDENT: every entry is defined relative to",
      "the printer's ArUco marker; all robot-specific geometry lives in TF and",
      "robot_config, never here.",
      "1) 'pos' entries are GRIPPER-TCP poses in the MARKER frame (frame=grasp).",
      "   At runtime the flange target is back-solved through the eef->TCP",
      "   transform from TF (robot_config 'grasp_frame', e.g. link_tcp), so the",
      "   same numbers put the FINGERTIPS in the same place on any arm.",
      "2) 'scan'/'move' entries position the CAMERA, not the wrist: the camera",
      "   optical frame is placed at the viewing distance along the marker",
      "   normal and the flange is back-solved through the eef->camera transform",
      "   from TF (plus the calibrate_camera_offset correction). 'Scan at 0.15'",
      "   therefore means the camera sits 0.15 m from the marker on every robot,",
      "   wherever its camera is mounted.",
      "3) The measured marker pose itself is corrected through the same camera",
      "   TF, so different robots scanning the same marker resolve the same",
      "   base-frame pose - the input to (1) is robot-agnostic too.",
      "4) 'gripper_width' entries are physical jaw openings in METERS, mapped",
      "   per robot via open_width/closed_width in robot_config; 'gripper'",
      "   fractions (0=open..1=closed) and 'open'/'close' also work.",
      "5) 'entry_zone_collisions' toggles only this printer's boxes flagged",
      "   'entry_zone': true (the volumes the gripper may enter mid-procedure).",
      "The original numbers were converted from the legacy lite6-tuned flange",
      "lists by removing the lite6's 0.0836 m flange->TCP offset."
    ],
